<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederic Thesiger, 2nd Baron Chelmsford</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1827">1827</a>–<a href="/years/1905">1905</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Lord Chelmsford</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederic Thesiger, 2nd Baron Chelmsford, was a British general who commanded the invasion of Zululand in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-zulu-war">Anglo-Zulu War</a> of 1879. His divided columns suffered the disaster at Isandlwana in January, but he restored his reputation in part by defeating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulu-kingdom">Zulu</a> army at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulundi">Ulundi</a> in July, shortly before he was superseded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garnet-wolseley">Sir Garnet Wolseley</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederic-thesiger-2nd-baron-chelmsford.jpg" alt="Frederic Thesiger, 2nd Baron Chelmsford" width="320" height="375" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Samuel Robert Lock / George C. Whitfield / Adam Cuerden · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Frederic_Thesiger,_Lord_Chelmsford.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
